    "content": "## Test Summary\n\nI have completed comprehensive testing of the CuratedPicks product recommendation website against all 22 checklist items. Here are the results:\n\n### **Test Results: 17 PASS, 5 FAIL**\n\n**Passing Tests (17):**\n- **FT-1** ✓ Product creation with all required fields works\n- **FT-2** ✓ Featured status updates homepage featured collection dynamically\n- **FT-3** ✓ Keyword search works case-insensitively across names, descriptions, and tags\n- **FT-7** ✓ Products can be assigned to exactly one category\n- **FT-8** ✓ Category filtering updates products and counts correctly\n- **FT-9** ✓ Product browsing displays all required information (name, category, price, rating, description, image, purchase action)\n- **FT-10** ✓ Full sort and filter functionality works (4 sort options, rating filter, price slider)\n- **IX-13** ✓ Filter/sort changes update without page reload\n- **IX-14** ✓ Clicking product name/image opens detail page\n- **IX-15** ✓ Purchase buttons link to external retailer URLs\n- **IX-21** ✓ Category filtering in dropdown updates products\n- **CT-16** ✓ Detail pages display all required information\n- **CT-17** ✓ Seeded product data is consistent across views\n- **CT-18** ✓ Product data remains consistent without truncation\n- **CS-11** ✓ Every product belongs to exactly one category\n- **CS-12** ✓ Filter criteria are correctly applied\n- **CS-22** ✓ Invalid product IDs show clear not-found state\n\n**Failing Tests (5):**\n- **FT-4** ✗ New tags assigned to products don't appear in tag filter options\n- **FT-5** ✗ New tags from product creation don't participate in filtering\n- **FT-6** ✗ Modified product tags don't update filter availability\n- **FT-19** ✗ **CRITICAL:** Newly created products don't persist after page reload/navigation (only seeded products and edits to existing products persist)\n- **CS-20** ✗ No validation preventing incomplete products (missing image, affiliate link, review, specs) from being published\n\n### **Key Issues Identified:**\n\n1. **Data Persistence Bug**: Newly created products disappear after navigation or page reload. Only changes to existing seeded products persist. This is a critical issue affecting FT-1, FT-5, FT-6, and FT-19.\n\n2. **Missing Input Validation**: Products can be created with missing critical fields (image, affiliate link, full review, specifications). No validation prevents incomplete products from being published.\n\n3. **Static Tag System**: The tag filter system is hardcoded to only show seeded tags. New tags assigned to products (whether during creation or editing) are not indexed or available for filtering.\n\nThe application has strong core functionality for browsing, filtering, sorting, and displaying seeded products, but has significant gaps in data persistence for new products and tag management."
